card.statement:
Let $\FF$ be a skew field that is finite dimensional over its center. Let $a\mapsto a^{\co}$ be an involutory automorphism of $\FF$ $($which can be the identity$)$. Let

\begin{equation}
A_iX_{i'}^{\alpha_i }-
X_{i''}^{\beta_i}B_i=C_i,\qquad i=1,\dots,s
\end{equation}

be a system of matrix equations over $\FF$ with unknown matrices $X_1,\dots,X_t$, in which all $\alpha_i,\beta_i\in\{1,\co\}$. Then the system <<ref:fbi>> has a solution if and only if there exist nonsingular matrices $P_1,\dots,P_t$ such that

\begin{equation}
\mat{A_i&0\\0&B_i}P_{i'}^{\alpha_i}
=P_{i''}^{\beta_i}\mat{A_i&C_i\\0&B_i},\qquad i=1,\dots,s.
\end{equation}
